steps.text:
Hard training and life stress both switch on the same stress pathways, which carry [cortisol](g:cortisol) and other hormones to immune cells [[c:stress-axes]]. So exam stress or a bad week at work adds to the training load.

Four levers follow:

- protect sleep ([sleep hygiene](g:sleep-hygiene)); sleep helps recovery, though data on how sleep loss changes athletes' immunity are thin [[c:sleep-thin]];
- eat enough, since [low energy availability](g:low-energy-availability) is a risk factor;
- manage life stress;
- take extra care in intensive weeks, in the taper and at competition [[c:risk-weeks]].
